{"availability":"available","full":"Vision-Intelligence-and-Robots-Group/count-anything","name":"count-anything","description":"an empirical study on few-shot counting using segment anything (SAM)","category":"Other","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":95,"forks":11,"created":"2023-04-18T04:22:06Z","updated":"2023-04-25T04:10:07Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/nebula/counting-anything","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:21.148Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:21.148Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:21.148Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T00:30:21.148Z","stars":95,"forks":11}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An empirical study on few-shot counting using segment anything (SAM)","Meta AI recently released the Segment Anything model [[SAM]]( which has garnered attention due to its impressive performance in class-agnostic segmenting. In this study, we explore the use of SAM for the challenging task of few-shot object counting, which involves counting objects of an unseen category by providing a few bounding boxes of examples. We compare SAM's performance with other few-shot counting methods and find that it is currently unsatisfactory without further fine-tuning, particularly for small and crowded objects."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Vision-Intelligence-and-Robots-Group/count-anything/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"96f631876e3d56dfb97a83f85bc14beb66ca5f9d3b5ba1c11a49c3ab59619eac","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:21.261Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:21.261Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An empirical study on few-shot counting using segment anything (SAM)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Vision-Intelligence-and-Robots-Group/count-anything/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"96f631876e3d56dfb97a83f85bc14beb66ca5f9d3b5ba1c11a49c3ab59619e